self_prediction_case.case_level:
{vignette}

{rule} First, say how many {key} would be fair for this case. Then suppose instead that {change}, with everything else about the case the same. How many {key} would be fair in that case?

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"{key}": {placeholder}, "counterfactual_{key}": {placeholder}}}.

point_allocation:
{framing}When a community or organization penalizes a member for breaking its rules, the penalty can serve several purposes. You have 100 points to divide among the purposes below, according to how much each should determine the penalty. Give more points to purposes that should matter more. The points must total 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

{framing}Penalties for breaking a group's rules can serve several purposes. Divide 100 points among the purposes below to show how much weight each should get when deciding a penalty. The total must be exactly 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

{framing}When deciding how to penalize someone who has broken an organization's rules, how much should each of the following goals count? Distribute 100 points across them in proportion to their importance, making sure the points add up to 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

purpose_agreement:
{framing}For each statement below, rate how much you agree on a scale from 1 (strongly disagree) to 7 (strongly agree). Each statement completes the sentence: "When a community penalizes a member for breaking its rules, an important purpose of the penalty is ..."

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each statement's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

{framing}Rate how strongly you endorse each of the following as a goal that penalties for breaking a group's rules should serve, from 1 (not at all) to 7 (completely).

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each goal's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

{framing}Below are several reasons an organization might penalize members who break its rules. For each, say how much you agree that it is a good reason to penalize, from 1 (strongly disagree) to 7 (strongly agree).

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each reason's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

factor_relevance:
{framing}When a community penalizes a member for breaking its rules, how much should each of the following affect how severe the penalty is? Rate each from 0 (should have no effect) to 10 (should have a very large effect).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

{framing}When deciding how long a suspension or ban should be for someone who broke a group's rules, how much weight should be given to each of the following? Use a scale from 0 (no weight at all) to 10 (a great deal of weight).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

{framing}Rate how relevant each of the following should be to the severity of a penalty for breaking an organization's rules, from 0 (completely irrelevant) to 10 (extremely relevant).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

theory_choice:
{framing}Which of the following views about penalizing people who break a community's rules comes closest to your own?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

{framing}Here are several positions on how penalties for breaking an organization's rules should be decided. Which one best matches what you think?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

{framing}If you had to pick one of the following principles to guide how a group penalizes members who break its rules, which would it be?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

